eplace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the 'typed non-applicable selection reason' — name the reason type (or enum) and enumerate its member value(s) (at minimum the scoped-glob-no-match case) that the snapshot records and the contract test asserts against.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.525,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A scoped glob that matches no changed path produces a typed non-applicable selection reason.'","AC: 'A nonmatching scoped glob records a typed non-applicable selection reason without executing the criterion.'","search_files 'selection reason' → (no matches): no existing typed reason vocabulary in repo to inherit from","Existing selection is a bare bool: registry.py:328 project_criterion_applies returns True/False with no reason payload"],"finding":"The plan repeatedly references a 'typed non-applicable selection reason' that a contract test must assert, but never defines the type name or its value vocabulary (what field/enum member a nonmatching scoped glob records). A grep for existing 'selection reason' vocabulary in the tree returns no matches, so it is net-new and unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4022d39ed3f3ec15","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach para 2 ('produces a typed non-applicable selection reason') and Acceptance Criteria line 'A nonmatching scoped glob records a typed non-applicable selection reason without executing the criterion.'","norm_id":"nd2fa205733680e9a","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A contract test asserting the non-applicable reason has no defined type/member to match against, so it may assert on an ad-hoc string that drifts from the compiler's emitted value","A consumer reading the snapshot cannot distinguish 'scoped-glob-no-match' from other non-applicable causes if only one untyped reason exists"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify exactly which state the snapshot digest incorporates (overlay bytes + packaged built-in/effective-index state + resolved operation inputs) so the digest is a faithful identity of the full effective view AC-1 promises, rather than only the overlay-bytes `_overlay_signature`.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.599,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["overlay.py:154-164 `_overlay_signature` = sha256 of overlay file bytes, returns \"\" when no overlay file","AC-1 requires the digest-bound view to contain 'effective built-in, project LLM, and project DET policy'","Plan word 'extends' is ambiguous about whether packaged-index/operation-input state is incorporated into the digest"],"finding":"The plan says the snapshot digest 'reuses/extends' the existing `_overlay_signature` content digest, but `_overlay_signature` hashes ONLY the overlay file bytes (it returns \"\" when no overlay is present). AC-1 requires the digest to bind the full effective view including packaged built-ins and resolved operation inputs. The plan does not specify whether/how the packaged-index and resolved-operation-input state are folded into the digest, so a digest that is purely overlay-bytes would not be a faithful identity of the compiled view (two different packaged/built-in states could collide on the same digest).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f86ccf605655308ae","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Alternatives-prior-art paragraph ('The CriteriaSnapshot digest reuses/extends that existing _overlay_signature content digest'); AC-1; AC-12","norm_id":"n421e6b80078a20c2","priority":0.201,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A built-in retune shipped in the packaged index changes the effective view but, if the digest is overlay-bytes-only, the digest is unchanged — two distinct effective views collide on one digest","The snapshot is described as derived under ADR 0098's OperationSnapshot resolved inputs, yet those inputs' contribution to the digest is unspecified"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that the CriteriaSnapshot digest is computed over the COMPILED effective view (effective built-ins after disables/retunes + project LLM + project DET + resolved operation inputs), using `_overlay_signature` as one input rather than the whole digest, so a packaged-built-in change or operation-input change is reflected in the digest.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_al